  "id": "COMPOUND:23867 - PROTEIN:83",
  "verbalization": "Fraxidin is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the Glucagon receptor through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Fraxidin acts as a target for the Prostaglandin D2 receptor, which in turn is targeted by another compound, 9-Hydroxy-12-oxo-10-octadecenoic acid. This chain of targets ultimately points to the Glucagon receptor as the final endpoint. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Fraxidin may influence the signaling of the Glucagon receptor through the Prostaglandin D2 receptor, possibly by modulating downstream signaling cascades. The evidence supports a role for Fraxidin in the regulation of the Glucagon receptor, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
